2.1.1 Requirements
------------------

   • *Emacs* 29.1 or later
   • *mpv* for live playback tracking
   • *eve CLI* for transcription and rendering (see below)
   • *FFmpeg with libass* and *fontconfig* (‘fc-match’) for burned-in
     captions; both tools are provided by this project's devenv
     environment
   • *hydra* (optional) for the ‘?’ keybinding cheatsheet popup


File: eve.info,  Node: Installing the CLI,  Next: Installing the Emacs package,  Prev: Requirements,  Up: Installation

2.1.2 Installing the CLI
------------------------

The Emacs package first looks for an ‘eve’ executable on your ‘PATH’.
If it does not find one, and ‘eve-cli-program’ is still set to its
default ‘"eve"’, it falls back to ‘scripts/run-cli.sh’ inside this
checkout.  That script creates a local virtualenv and installs the
pre-built wheel from ‘cli/dist/’.

   For standard in-Emacs use, that local bootstrap path means a separate
global ‘eve’ install is optional.  The fallback path assumes Python 3.12
or later is available and that the package checkout is writable.  It
reuses an existing ‘cli/.venv’; it does not automatically refresh that
environment when a new wheel is shipped.  After updating the package,
refresh an existing CLI installation using its original installation
method.  In a devenv development checkout, use the project's Python
synchronization workflow rather than replacing its managed environment
with a runtime wheel installation.

   If you want ‘eve’ on your ‘PATH’ for shell use, install it globally:

     pip install cli/dist/eve_cli-*.whl
     # or with uv:
     uv pip install cli/dist/eve_cli-*.whl

   Verify it works:

     eve doctor --json


