File: eve.info,  Node: Concept,  Next: Configuration (1),  Up: Filler Words

6.1 Concept
===========

Filler words ("um", "uh", "you know") clutter transcripts.  Eve's filler
workflow is non-destructive: words are _marked_ as fillers first, then
_optionally deleted_.  Marked fillers are highlighted in the buffer with
a distinct face and excluded from compilation.  You can mark a word as
non-filler for this TJM file so future auto-tagging leaves it alone.


File: eve.info,  Node: Configuration (1),  Next: Commands,  Prev: Concept,  Up: Filler Words

6.2 Configuration
=================

     ;; Plain strings — single words or multi-word phrases
     (setq eve-filler-phrases '("um" "uh" "you know" "to be honest with you"))

   ‘eve-filler-phrases’ stores phrases as plain strings.  Matching is
case-insensitive, punctuation-insensitive, and prefers the longest
phrase first.  For example, ‘"you know"’ matches adjacent words like
‘you know,’ and marks both words as a filler phrase; it does not mark
separated words such as ‘you ... know’.  Eve stores editable filler
decisions in ‘word.edit.filler’; legacy ‘word.edit.kind = "filler"’
metadata is still recognized.  The list is persisted when you use the
interactive add commands.

   ‘eve-filler-exception-phrases’ stores phrases that should not be
auto-marked as fillers.  Exceptions win over filler phrases: if ‘like’
is a filler but ‘would like’ is an exception, the ‘like’ in ‘would like’
stays non-filler.

   The legacy ‘eve-filler-regex’ variable is still honoured for
backwards compatibility but ‘eve-filler-phrases’ is preferred.


File: eve.info,  Node: Commands,  Next: Auto-tagging on file open,  Prev: Configuration (1),  Up: Filler Words

6.3 Commands
============

Key           Command                                     Description
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘f’           ‘eve-dwim-filler’                           Add the word at point to phrases and retag; or delete region as filler.
‘F’           ‘eve-delete-fillers’                        Mark all tagged fillers as deleted.
‘A’           ‘eve-accept-filler’                         Mark the filler at point as non-filler in this TJM file.
‘]f’ / ‘[f’   ‘eve-next-filler’ / ‘eve-previous-filler’   Jump to next / previous visible filler.
‘C-c C-d’     ‘eve-delete-fillers’                        Same as ‘F’ from the ‘C-c’ prefix map.
—             ‘M-x eve-tag-fillers’                       Mark all matching words in the buffer.
—             ‘M-x eve-add-filler-at-point’               Add the word at point to ‘eve-filler-phrases’ and retag.
—             ‘M-x eve-add-filler-region’                 Add the selected phrase to ‘eve-filler-phrases’ and retag.
—             ‘M-x eve-add-filler-exception’              Add the word/region as a future filler exception.


File: eve.info,  Node: Auto-tagging on file open,  Prev: Commands,  Up: Filler Words

6.4 Auto-tagging on file open
=============================

Fillers are tagged automatically every time a TJM manifest is opened.
If you add a new phrase to ‘eve-filler-phrases’, reopen the file or run
‘M-x eve-tag-fillers’ to apply the updated list.  Words explicitly
marked as non-filler with ‘A’ are persisted in the TJM file and are not
auto-tagged again.


