10.1 Timestamp ruler
====================

‘eve-ruler-mode’ (active by default) displays ‘[hh:mm:ss]’ markers in
the right margin.  Each marker is placed next to the segment that
_reaches_ that milestone in the rendered video — deleted content is
excluded from the running total.

   The total rendered duration appears in the mode line.

     ;; Change the milestone interval (default 30 seconds)
     (setq eve-ruler-interval 60.0)

   Toggle the ruler with ‘C-c C-l’ (‘eve-ruler-mode’).


File: eve.info,  Node: Context panels,  Next: Hiding deleted segments,  Prev: Timestamp ruler,  Up: Display

10.2 Context panels
===================

‘C-c C-p’ (‘eve-context-panels-open’) opens or refreshes the optional
Eve context UI when the ‘context-panels’ package is available.  It opens
the side panel plus the current-segment bottom editor, then focuses the
bottom panel for rapid review.  During the optional-first migration, Eve
continues to work without that package.

   Opening the side panel disables the legacy right-margin
‘eve-ruler-mode’ while the panel is active.  The side panel shows fixed
rendered-timeline timestamp landmarks using the same interval, anchored
to the corresponding visible transcript row when possible.  Internal
segment ids are intentionally hidden.  Segments and markers with b-roll
also get compact ‘🎞’ rows showing file basename, duration, and
configuration glyphs such as ‘▣’ replace, ‘⊕’ overlay, ‘◱’
picture-in-picture, ‘🎙’ source audio, ‘♪’ b-roll audio, ‘🔇’ mute, ‘→’
continue, ‘▧’ still, ‘{…}’ placeholders, and ‘▭’ overlays.

   The bottom panel is a current-segment cockpit.  It repeats the
canonical timed transcript words, shows segment timing/speaker/tags
state, b-roll status, and key-hinted action rows.  In the bottom panel,
‘w’ / ‘b’ move between visible words, ‘v’ toggles a panel-local word
selection, ‘j’ / ‘n’ and ‘k’ / ‘p’ move to next/previous segments while
keeping focus in the panel, ‘q’ returns focus to the source buffer, and
‘Q’ closes the bottom panel.  Panel selection is visual and does not
mutate the source buffer's region.

     ;; Enable local development integration outside eve.el itself.
     (add-to-list 'load-path "~/ws/context-panels")

   Set ‘eve-context-panels-auto-open’ to non-nil to open context panels
automatically when entering ‘eve-mode’.


File: eve.info,  Node: Hiding deleted segments,  Next: Word-level display,  Prev: Context panels,  Up: Display

10.3 Hiding deleted segments
============================

‘C-c C-h’ (‘eve-hide-deleted-mode’) toggles visibility of deleted words
and segments.  When active (the default), deleted content is hidden and
the transcript reads as it will render.  When inactive, deleted content
appears with a strikethrough face.


File: eve.info,  Node: Word-level display,  Prev: Hiding deleted segments,  Up: Display

